history=[(-600,'Lumen Tide already inhabited','Independent deep-water oral and written traditions describe a harbor civilization; no surface dynasty is made its founder.'),(-420,'Ossara’s three public wells','Three caravanning groups settle around distinct wells; their agreements become the basis of later public claims.'),(-360,'Warm refuge at Hushvale','Spring caverns support a permanent mountain community and early weather observation.'),(-310,'Stonewake terraces','Working quarries and shelter galleries become a town; later construction preserves some dangerous abandoned faces.'),(-280,'Nacre Quay rises','A new port grows above an older drowned district. The submergence is a separate geological event, not the Severance.'),(-240,'Reedbank ferry town','Boat crews and riverside households establish shared flood stairs and public food stores.'),(-220,'Millmere channels','Milling and instrument crafts establish a canal community.'),(-210,'The Open Ways mature','Local builders connect bridges, shelters, signals and limited waycraft. Exclusion and toll disputes exist alongside cooperation.'),(-190,'Kettle Crown founded','Cooled volcanic shelves and managed springs support a forge-and-garden settlement.'),(-180,'Latchford junction','Three maintained roads create a transfer town and a culture of route testimony.'),(-160,'Crownrest formed','Canopy communities establish adjustable crown decks and a fixed ridge refuge.'),(-145,'Willowmere grows','Growers settle the forest margin; seeds and teaching become shared institutions.'),(-130,'Aurel Quay charter','Mooring communities adopt cooperative load rules and prohibit ownership of residents through vessel contracts.'),(-92,'The Severance','A resonance-span cascade threatens connected crossings. Routekeepers deliberately cut some couplings to prevent wider collapse. Other roads fail later through weather, conflict and neglect.'),(-91,'After the cuts','Some closed routes are necessary; others remain closed because toll interests and fearful institutions benefit. No single actor controls the whole network.'),(-75,'Cinder freight district','New freight terraces provide work, then grow into mixed households and repair shops.'),(-18,'The freight diversion','A new line enriches Kettle Crown and reduces Cinder Cuts work. Political decisions, not a monster attack, create this grievance.'),(-9,'Stonewake platform failure','Nineteen-year-old Gorilla tries to hold a failing work platform rather than insisting on evacuation. Eris is injured and recovers; responsibility is recorded.'),(-8,'Bot activated','Lume and the Millmere cooperative build a learning maintenance person. Agency grows through relationships and choices.'),(-7,'Reedbank flood','Madger overpromises transport for eighteen households; a second convoy saves everyone. Veyra’s concealed funding and Sela’s agreement become a later revelation.'),(-6,'Burrow foundation','Madger and a voluntary group establish a camp and common store. Surveyors and builders document existing rock, water and entries before expansion. Gorilla joins in the first year.'),(-5,'Bot joins; first major inhabited galleries','Bot chooses records and maintenance work. Iona’s later team inherits documented systems, not a forgotten magical machine.'),(-4,'Neighborhood institutions mature','Workshops, food exchange, teaching and care expand with households; Mara, Jun and Edda arrive through ordinary work and family decisions.'),(-3,'Snow chooses a new home','Asha retires. Gradual placement with Madger succeeds, with continuing visits. Occupied underground wards expand within surveyed allocations.'),(-2,'Tavi arrives','An apprentice household settles West Deep. The town is established enough to give younger residents ambitions beyond survival.'),(0,'Pilot baseline','Late spring. Two populated districts, 2,400 planning residents, public access and independent inner defenses. The repaired bridge is sound. Joy precedes subtle clues.')]
world['history']=[{'year':y,'event':t,'truth':v} for y,t,v in history]
world['burrow_construction']=[{'phase':'Year -6','work':'Camp, survey, common store and temporary work platforms. Existing rock galleries are mapped before habitation. No ancient machine creates the town.'},{'phase':'Years -5 to -4','work':'Surface housing and civic services grow alongside the first reinforced inhabited galleries. Water, air, waste and access are installed before each occupancy increment.'},{'phase':'Years -3 to -1','work':'Four underground wards and shared civic rooms reach the present layout. Builders reuse documented connections; no undisclosed bypass is invented.'},{'phase':'Pilot','work':'All 37 primary areas and seven detailed subplans match v2.1. The town maintains rather than magically expands its capacity.'}]

site_rows=[
('SITE-01','Floodglass Ford','REG-01',18,-26,120,80,'Reedbank–Latchford river branch','A shallow crossing beside a fixed high-water refuge; reeds hide a second abandoned channel.','Flood-wyrm spawning and sudden flow changes.','A traveler’s missing wagon is found upstream of the place its record claims.','Two visible shore approaches; high refuge on north bank; no hidden tunnel.'),
('SITE-02','Walking Root Crossing','REG-02',82,105,160,120,'Willowmere–Crownrest guide route','Three living root spans cross a ravine; an anchored ridge hut holds tools and dry supplies.','Crown migration stretches lashings; mawroot plants imitate sheltered warmth off the marked path.','Madger must choose between pursuing Nix and catching a slipping wagon.','Ridge west, crown east; two fall-arrest anchor stations and a lower rescue shelf.'),
('SITE-03','The Buried Lens','REG-03',212,40,100,100,'Ossara western dune circuit','A sunken optical chamber and four exposed shafts below a circular storm court.','Glass storm, reflected false bearings, glassback drake nests.','A light impression disproves one story but cannot identify who created the scene.','One excavated stair and a separate maintenance ramp; shafts are light wells, not walkable escape holes.'),
('SITE-04','Drowned Archive','REG-04',172,-172,120,90,'Nacre Quay inner reef','A submerged civic hall exposed near low tide; records survive in upper dry cells.','Rising water, unstable floors and a passing reefback.','A salvage prize is evidence belonging to living families.','Upper landing and two raised exits remain above the expected low-tide window; boats are staged outside.'),
('SITE-05','Blackwake Mooring','REG-05',250,145,160,100,'Aurel Quay eastern flight lane','An abandoned counterweight platform with three small pirate craft and a repair gantry.','Wind shear, overloaded spans and hostage coercion.','Eri must use a former rescue captain’s own loading rules against his ransom scheme.','Three docking arms, two refuge cells, exposed winch deck; no infinite aircraft hangar.'),
('SITE-06','The Cut Span','REG-06',-70,242,180,100,'Hushvale southern ridge','A deliberately severed resonance bridge with two inspection houses and a visible gap.','Real coupled resonance hazard and choirwraith territory beyond the marked ridge.','A forged closure is exposed beside a genuine closure that must stay in force.','North and south abutments are separate; a safe foot detour takes two days and does not reconnect the span.'),
('SITE-07','Ashmouth Freight Yard','REG-07',-142,-43,180,120,'Cinder Cuts eastern spur','Raider-controlled storage and a former loading platform; occupied civilian terraces are elsewhere.','Ashmaws follow heat plumes; gang patrols guard movable stolen freight.','Dreg refuses an order to burn supplies and splits the crew.','One wagon approach, one narrow foot path, fenced gas trough; both routes are mapped.'),
('SITE-08','Bellwater Narrows','REG-08',-43,65,200,120,'Lumen Tide outer harbor','Two rock piers bracket a tidal channel, with a sheltered upper refuge ledge.','Bell-eels hunt vibration; pressure change can close the water route.','Namu must decide how much of a protected chart to share during a rescue.','Sea approaches east and west, foot access south to the refuge, no route to the Burrow.')]
for r in site_rows:world['sites'].append(dict(zip(['id','name','region','x','y','width_m','height_m','approach','appearance','hazard','story','layout'],r)))

creatures=[('CR-01','Flood-wyrm','REG-01','Long slate river animal with reedlike whiskers and four small paddle limbs.','Spawns in shallow reed beds; feeds on river mollusks.','Responds to disturbance, not evil intent; upstream silt curls and stripped reeds warn of presence.','Give spawning grounds room and use high crossings; cannot burrow through stone.'),('CR-02','Mawroot','REG-02','Root colony with amber cup flowers and fibrous folding leaves.','Captures small animals with warm sheltered hollows during cold rain.','Warmth lure has a short range; cut fibers cannot rapidly regrow.','Guides recognize sweet resin without leaf mold; stepping back breaks the trap before it closes.'),('CR-03','Glassback drake','REG-03','Low six-limbed lizard with overlapping translucent back plates.','Nests beneath stable glass crust and eats salt beetles.','Senses ground vibration; dazzling plates reflect light but do not fire beams.','Move on bedrock, avoid nest bowls and wait out a threat display.'),('CR-04','Reefback','REG-04','Huge slow shelled sea animal carrying living reef gardens.','Migrates between feeding grounds; young shelter near warmer shallows.','Can wreck a careless mooring without aggression; migration changes local currents.','Reef tenders post seasonal channels; no riding one as an obedient vehicle.'),('CR-05','Storm manta','REG-05','Wide amber-gray glider with fin ribbons and luminous throat spots.','Feeds on airborne spores and follows predictable pressure fronts.','Wing turbulence threatens light craft; it cannot summon a storm.','Sail crews read ribbon position and give the feeding column space.'),('CR-06','Choirwraith','REG-06','Pale translucent mothlike cave predator with resonant throat membranes.','Mimics recently heard sounds to draw prey toward sheltered ice pockets.','Copies fragments, not a dead person’s mind; warmth weakens the membranes.','Verify a voice with an agreed visual signal and retreat to warm refuge.'),('CR-07','Ashmaw','REG-07','Low armored burrower with charcoal plates and a glowing orange mouth lining.','Tracks heat in mineral soils and scavenges kiln waste.','Follows thermal gradients, cannot swim through liquid lava or survive any heat.','Divert cooled waste carefully and keep travelers away from fresh vents.'),('CR-08','Bell-eel','REG-08','Long translucent eel with mineral-rimmed resonator chambers.','Hunts vibration in deep channels and nests in quiet rock pockets.','Sound carries far through water; light alone does not repel it.','Reduce hull impacts, use known quiet passages and avoid nesting seasons.'),('CR-09','Sailfin packbeast','REG-03','Six-legged dune herbivore with a foldable cooling sail and broad padded feet.','Domestic herds graze salt grass near oasis margins.','Needs water and rest; refuses unstable glass crust.','Caravan teams treat refusal as information, not disobedience.'),('CR-10','Moss lantern beetle','REG-02','Palm-sized green beetle with a soft amber abdomen and leaflike wing cases.','Pollinates night flowers; light indicates mating and temperature.','Light fades when cold or stressed; not an endless lamp battery.','Residents use shaded observation gardens and leave wild colonies intact.'),('CR-11','Deep sail snail','REG-08','Large pale marine snail with a ridged buoyant shell and trailing sensory fronds.','Grazes floating fungal mats; empty shells become instruments.','Living shells are fragile; removing them kills the animal.','Harvest only shed mineral fragments and naturally empty shells.'),('CR-12','Ridge ram','REG-06','Shaggy blue-gray mountain herbivore with broad spiral horns.','Moves along stable ridge shelves and shelters near warm stone.','Defends a narrow path when calves are nearby; not innately hostile.','Wait at marked widening points and let the herd pass.')]
world['creatures']=[dict(zip(['id','name','region','look','ecology','limit','encounter'],x)) for x in creatures]

world['waycraft']=[{'name':'Resonant spans','rule':'Coupled stone and metal structures can share loads only within a measured local frequency and material condition. Damage can propagate through a coupled chain. Cutting a coupling stops transmission but closes that route.','cost':'Inspection, tuned materials and locally powered mechanisms; reconnection is a tested engineering choice, not a spell.'},{'name':'Canopy shaping','rule':'Slow cultivation encourages living fibers; full bridges take growing seasons. Guide songs encode timing and work sequences, not mind control.','cost':'Water, trained care and seasonal limits. Fire or rapid cutting permanently damages a tree.'},{'name':'Mirage glass','rule':'Certain glass layers retain partial light impressions under rare conditions. They show fragments from an angle, without sound, intent or guaranteed dates.','cost':'Careful extraction, controlled light and comparison with independent evidence.'},{'name':'Liftstone','rule':'Specific basalt inclusions respond to local field zones in the Saffron Isles. Load, anchor field and weather determine stable altitude.','cost':'Counterweights and inspection; ore moved beyond a field does not float freely.'},{'name':'Echo ice','rule':'Layered mineral ice stores and repeats sound fragments under pressure changes. Sounds can overlap or be misordered.','cost':'Cold preservation and expert interpretation; no resurrection or reading minds.'},{'name':'Ordinary technology','rule':'Relays, instruments and local networks coexist with hand tools and sail transport. A message is a claim; a physical latch is independent.','cost':'Power, maintenance, specific access and local knowledge. No universal instant map or hacking power.'}]
world['everyday_world']=[{'topic':'Peoples and personhood','text':'Communities are mixed-species societies. Species affects anatomy and some needs, never moral allegiance. Mechanical persons have agency. Ordinary animals such as Snow and wildlife remain distinct from anthropomorphic citizens. No human population is introduced in this edition.'},{'topic':'Food and trade','text':'Grains, roots, fruits, cultivated fungi, legumes and regional fish support distinct cuisines. Cargo has weight and spoilage. Each community’s imports explain its partnerships; no city survives solely by selling secrets. Fictional small coin and barter appear without tying plot prices to a real token.'},{'topic':'Home and family','text':'Households include relatives, chosen family, apprentices and solitary residents. A home has privacy, storage, food preparation and a way to receive visitors. New arrivals come for work, affection, curiosity and retirement as well as displacement.'},{'topic':'Languages and stories','text':'A common trade tongue permits travel, while local names, songs and technical terms need interpretation. Writing is widespread but not universal. Records, oral histories and physical evidence can disagree without making an entire culture dishonest.'},{'topic':'Faith and memory','text':'Communities hold different beliefs about rivers, ancestors, stars and the deep sea. No narrator proves a single religion correct. Festivals can be joyful, comic or solemn and need not conceal a villain.'},{'topic':'Law and conflict','text':'Local councils, tribunals and craft agreements differ. Captured offenders face community-specific proceedings rather than automatic execution. Good institutions can make mistakes; enemies may tell truths. No faction represents every member of a species or region.'},{'topic':'Scale and wonder','text':'The inhabited atlas spans hundreds of kilometres and large height differences. A voyage creates separation, missed news and new relationships. Strange environments have economies and children and meals, not only dangers waiting for heroes.'},{'topic':'Continuity','text':'The pilot remains entirely inside the Burrow and shows no villain identity. New geography becomes available afterward. Each scene records location, route, elapsed time, knowledge, injuries, resources and changes. Game retries are not historical resurrection.'}]

# Route definitions are explicit fictional travel baselines, not straight-line teleports.
edges=[('BRW','EXT-03','road',34,2,'East public gate joins an exterior approach at regional (1.5,0); the Burrow interior graph is unchanged.'),('EXT-03','EXT-01','road',48,3,'Raised river causeway; flood season can close the lower branch.'),('EXT-01','EXT-04','river',58,2,'One upstream day plus docking and current allowance.'),('EXT-03','EXT-04','road',44,3,'Canal service road with one staffed overnight yard.'),('BRW','EXT-02','road',78,5,'Departure still uses the existing east gate, then the exterior ring road turns northwest; no new western gate.'),('EXT-03','EXT-05','road',82,5,'Forest-margin road via fixed ridge farms.'),('EXT-05','EXT-07','guided forest',100,6,'Spring route; local guides update root crossings. Wet-season detour adds two days.'),('EXT-04','EXT-08','caravan',200,12,'Two water stops and a storm reserve; walking convoy pace applies.'),('EXT-08','EXT-09','caravan',230,14,'Dry plateau to coast with two transfer days.'),('EXT-09','EXT-10','sky',340,5,'One weather wait and one load/transfer day; only in safe conditions.'),('EXT-08','EXT-10','sky',130,3,'Two transfer/weather days included; finite scheduled craft.'),('EXT-02','EXT-11','mountain',240,15,'Winter closure possible; ridge wayhouses and slower ascent.'),('EXT-02','EXT-06','road',150,9,'Freight approach has public and raider-controlled branches.'),('EXT-06','EXT-12','road',46,3,'Basalt freight terraces; gas closure adds a day.'),('EXT-02','EXT-13','descent',16,2,'Dedicated Stonewake descent and pressure/air checks; 1,920 m vertical change. No Burrow connection.'),('EXT-13','SITE-08','boat',3,1,'Local boat excursion; safe tide and quiet channel required.')]
world['routes']=[dict(zip(['a','b','mode','length_km','days','conditions'],x),id=f'WAY-{i+1:02d}') for i,x in enumerate(edges)]

# Season one is inherited, with later seasons structured as complete local arcs.
world['seasons']=[{'number':1,'title':'The Missing Roads','question':'Can a welcoming home defend itself without becoming dependent on someone else’s power?','episodes':story['episodes'],'ending':'Missing travelers rescued; raid repelled; trust damaged by real disclosures; Nix escapes after one limited act of repair. The Burrow chooses accountable outward partnerships.'}]
season2=[('A Map That Drinks','Ossara','Maela asks the travelers to verify a well claim; a glass storm destroys the easy route home.','Madger accepts local leadership.'),('The Price of Shade','Ossara','Kavar offers water in exchange for exclusive certificates; the group shelters in a public court.','Gorilla cannot solve scarcity by carrying more.'),('The Buried Lens','SITE-03','A light impression appears to condemn Maela’s family; its angle proves the scene has been misread.','Bot states what the image cannot establish.'),('A Table for Strangers','Ossara','A feast and comic cooking rivalry reveal whose labor maintains the public wells.','A quiet bond replaces an exposition speech.'),('Below the Tide','Nacre Quay','Toma takes the team to a drowned archive where the decisive record belongs to descendants.','Madger gives up a claim he could legally seize.'),('The Captain’s Copy','Nacre Quay','Toma’s stolen chart is exposed; a rival crew gets the rescue credit.','Toma returns evidence without demanding praise.'),('Home Is Busy','The Burrow','Mara, Jun and Pell resolve a festival dispute while the heroes are away.','The town proves capable without its founder.'),('Water for No One','Ossara','Kavar’s debt forgery is proven, but the pump remains physically damaged.','Victory requires repair and collective allocation.'),('The Open Court','Ossara','Public testimony and a difficult rebuild restore limited supply.','Maela lets neighbors set the rules.'),('What the Map Leaves Out','Reedbank','The travelers return with a route to Hushvale and news that some closures saved lives.','Madger chooses a harder question over a triumphant legend.')]
season3=[('Weight of a Promise','Aurel Quay','Eri refuses an overloaded departure and loses a prestigious contract.','Gorilla respects a public refusal.'),('The Kind Captain','SITE-05','Serik rescues stranded passengers and then demands permanent tribute.','The team separates real skill from moral authority.'),('Three Islands, One Storm','Aurel Quay','Rescue priorities divide dock crews as migration weather approaches.','Eri launches with a bounded plan and turns back once.'),('A Song Without Purpose','Aurel Quay','Bot composes music with sailmakers during repairs.','He enjoys something nobody needs him to optimize.'),('The Voice in the Ice','Hushvale','An echo seems to accuse the original routekeepers of betrayal.','Ysolde distinguishes sequence from interpretation.'),('The Necessary Cut','SITE-06','Independent measurements prove one closure still prevents a cascade.','Madger abandons a simple reopening campaign.'),('The Forged Winter','Hushvale','Ossa’s modern forged order is exposed beside genuine records.','Ysolde publishes her own family’s benefit too.'),('Who Gets to Decide','Hushvale','The archive order splits; local communities demand a role in testing.','Expertise remains essential without becoming rule.'),('A Smaller Bridge','Stonewake','A limited new crossing succeeds without reconnecting the dangerous chain.','Gorilla teaches Tavi and accepts Eris’s lead.'),('The Road We Choose','The Burrow','The team returns with a treaty of limited reciprocal routes.','The world remains complex, but more people can shape their future.')]
season4=[('The Letter Below','Stonewake','Namu invites an exchange after an old chart reappears.','Bot asks what sharing requires.'),('Down Through Daylight','EXT-13','A careful descent introduces an independent deep civilization.','Madger becomes a guest.'),('The City on the Water','Lumen Tide','A harbor festival reveals rival accounts of the city’s origins.','No single record decides belonging.'),('Quiet Hull','SITE-08','A rescue among bell-eels requires silence and patience.','Snow remains on the safe shore with a familiar handler.'),('The Mineral Claim','Lumen Tide','A surface syndicate uses an old charter to demand extraction.','Toma renounces a profitable inherited claim.'),('No One’s Discovery','Lumen Tide','Residents show the heroes that their map already names the supposedly lost shore.','The expedition changes its language and purpose.'),('Heat and Distance','Kettle Crown','Kesh negotiates work with neglected Cinder Cuts families.','Apology precedes the new machine.'),('A Captain Without a Crew','Cinder Cuts','Brakka’s band fractures over burned supplies and unpaid shares.','Dreg returns a victim ledger and accepts consequences.'),('The Shared Passage','Stonewake','Partners establish a narrow, accountable trade route.','Namu shares enough to cooperate while retaining boundaries.'),('A Place to Return To','The Burrow','Visitors from several regions share an ordinary meal and exchange future invitations.','Home grows through relationships, not conquest.')]
for no,title,q,eps,end in [(2,'Glass and Tides','Who owns a discovery?',season2,'A public well restored, a stolen chart returned and a community given control of its own evidence.'),(3,'The Necessary Cut','When does protection become control?',season3,'A dangerous closure remains; a forged one falls; a limited safe crossing replaces the fantasy of reopening everything.'),(4,'The Sea Beneath','Can exchange happen without possession?',season4,'A reciprocal deep-world partnership and a fractured raiding network create a new political landscape.')]:
 world['seasons'].append({'number':no,'title':title,'question':q,'episodes':[{'number':f'{i+1:02d}','title':e[0],'setting':e[1],'plot':e[2],'character_turn':e[3]} for i,e in enumerate(eps)],'ending':end})
world['standalone_stories']=[{'title':a,'cast':b,'plot':c} for a,b,c in [('The Empty Chair','Gorilla, Edda, Mara','Everyone leaves Gorilla a plate and nobody notices he has missed every meal. He must name his limit; friends must change the work, not merely deliver food.'),('The Wrong Song','Neri, Senn, Lark','A route song is performed beautifully with one practical verse missing. The failure becomes a lesson in learning from people, not collecting exotic art.'),('The Painted Door','Jun, Pell, Pip','A repaired door carries a former family’s mark. Ownership of the object and ownership of the memory pull in different directions.'),('Snow’s Long Morning','Snow, Asha, Madger','A largely wordless walk follows an innocent smell, a lost glove and a tired visitor. The audience learns to read her pauses before the people do.'),('The Cup That Leaked','Kesh, Tavi, Oren','A contest rewards an elegant cup until it is filled. The apprentice who admits a flaw wins no prize but earns a better commission.'),('When the Founder Visits','Dara, Hollis, Madger','Madger returns to Reedbank expecting to help and finds a community busy without him. He must learn how to be a son on a quiet day.'),('One Honest Bargain','Pip, Lark, Pell','Pip returns an object and loses three customers. Building a lawful stall is less glamorous and harder than one dramatic confession.'),('The Unnecessary Tune','Bot, Lume','Bot shares a piece of music. Lume begins to debug it before realizing he wanted her to listen.'),('A Night Without Lamps','Namu, Toma','A planned dark festival becomes a comic navigation problem for surface visitors; local expertise solves it before danger is invented.'),('Seeds for a Rival','Sori, Iona, Maela','A failed harvest experiment can be saved only by sharing seeds with a competitor who was correct about its limits.'),('The Faster Letter','Lark, Tessera','A correction must catch a false story before a caravan acts. Lark wins by admitting her own role, while Tessera abandons a profitable identity.'),('The Better Builder','Gorilla, Eris','A sibling contest becomes a public credit dispute. The winning structure is the one whose builders can explain each other’s contribution.')]]

world['reveal_ledger']=[{'truth':'Veyra funded the second flood convoy','plant':'Sela avoids one charter question; a depot mark appears on a rescue invoice.','proof':'Independent charter account plus boat operator testimony.','payoff':'Madger rejects ownership claims while acknowledging a real rescue.','audience':'Season 1 midpoint; absent from pilot.'},{'truth':'Nix leads Glass Thread','plant':'Familiar knot and copper clamp; partial route language Madger remembers.','proof':'Direct encounter and corroborated relay evidence.','payoff':'Rescue versus pursuit; friendship becomes a difficult future possibility.','audience':'Season 1 midpoint.'},{'truth':'D17 is Tessera’s limited relay test','plant':'A duplicate receipt with a bounded inconsistency.','proof':'Source comparison and a physical access witness.','payoff':'The town distinguishes corrupted messages from mechanical control.','audience':'Later season 1; pilot shows only discrepancy.'},{'truth':'Some closures prevented catastrophe','plant':'Cut couplings, contradictory archive fragments and surviving inspection marks.','proof':'Independent measurements and records from more than one community.','payoff':'A limited new crossing replaces indiscriminate reopening.','audience':'Season 3.'},{'truth':'Ossa forged a modern closure order','plant':'Material and dating conflict in a record that is otherwise technically credible.','proof':'Original archive copy, witness and field comparison.','payoff':'Institutional reform without discarding genuine expertise.','audience':'Season 3.'}]
world['production_contract']={'images':'Art plates control palette, material vocabulary, costume and silhouette. Dimensioned plans and JSON control coordinates, counts, doors and connections. Resolve a mismatch by correcting the image, never silently moving the plan.','animation':'Use held poses, selected key poses and separate mouth/expression layers. Do not regenerate whole bodies for every mouth frame. Keep fixed camera backgrounds, matched eyelines, deliberate face close-ups and consistent silhouettes.','voices':burrow['voice_reference'],'hero_scale':'New staging heights are production assumptions for this atlas, not replacements for approved body proportions. Scale uniformly; never stretch an approved model to fit a height.','new_voice_policy':'Supporting voices remain unassigned until selected; this atlas does not spend ElevenLabs or Runway credits.','models':'Each character retains stable ID, anatomy, height, palette, signature prop and silhouette. Each environment retains local origin, district boundaries, building instances and state overlays.','completion_boundary':'This edition supplies a complete interconnected foundation for the named cast and principal atlas locations. Generic blocks use reusable measured modules; they are not falsely represented as thousands of individually decorated interiors. Future named rooms and minor settlements require additive sheets.'}
assert len(world['characters'])==40 and len(world['communities'])==14
(OUT/'World_Atlas.json').write_text(json.dumps(world,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
print('Authored',len(world['characters']),'characters,',len(world['communities']),'communities,',len(world['factions']),'factions')
